00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:16.409
Let's start with Dorne for anyone who's
all like WTF Martells. Most of what we know

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:21.229
about Dorne from the show is that House Martell
rules there and they still have a prince,

00:01:21.229 --> 00:01:26.539
Oberyn Martell's older brother Doran. I
already explained why Dorne gets a prince

00:01:26.539 --> 00:01:30.789
and the other seven kingdoms only have Lords,
but basically it's because they resisted

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:34.140
Aegon's Conquest. They were just extra badass.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.630
In the first couple of episodes this season,
Oberyn kind of let slip little facts about

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:44.630
Dorne's culture. For instance, they don't
hold women as subservient to men. For instance,

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:49.490
if Brienne lived there she could be a Knight
no problem. There wouldn't be any gender

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:54.659
inequality. And if Cersei had been born there,
she would get the status a male heir would

00:01:54.659 --> 00:01:54.859
get.

00:01:54.859 --> 00:01:59.880
Oberyn himself is something of a sexual omnivore
just humping his way across the world. But

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.960
in general, people are much more openly promiscuous
there. Including the noble women. So where

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:09.229
Cersei would be called a whore for sleeping
with a bunch of men in King's Landing, were

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:15.610
she in Dorne. There wouldn't be as much
of a stigma.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.500
The First Men actually settled Westeros by
crossing a land bridge that extended from

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.260
Dorne to the eastern continent. But during
their war with the Children of the Forest,

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:28.390
it's said the Children broke the Land Bridge
to keep more people from coming.

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:35.390
Dorne's culture is mostly influenced by
Rhoynar, they were people that were defeated

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:42.659
by the Valyrian Freehold about a thousand
years before the events on the show. Those

00:02:42.659 --> 00:02:46.750
people sailed with like 10 thousand men to
Dorne, their leader Nymeria, the same name

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:53.750
as Arya's Direwolf, made a pact with the
Martells and they conquered the area that

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.909
would become modern day Dorne.

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:01.900
So a lot of the Rhoynar culture sank in.

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:07.379
The current falling out between Dorne and
the Crown is mostly related to the Lannisters.

00:03:07.379 --> 00:03:12.610
Specifically Tywin Lannister over the fate
of Princess Elia. She was Prince Doran and

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.640
Oberyn's sister who was married to Rhaegar
Targaryen.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:20.250
That's the person Oberyn was talking about
the Mountain murdering during Robert's Rebellion

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:24.250
and the sack of King's Landing.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.819
Supposedly the Mountain was only doing it
on the orders of Tywin Lannister, since he's

00:03:28.819 --> 00:03:33.480
one of Tywin's bannermen. Prince Doran also
suspects the same thing as Oberyn, so he's

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:39.049
allowing Oberyn to learn more about what happened.
Although the murdering spree Oberyn teased

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:43.420
is just him going above and beyond the call
of duty in the name of revenge.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:48.159
Which is where we are as of Episode 8.

00:03:48.159 --> 00:03:54.840
Moving on to Season 5 News. Mostly Dorne related.
The crew was spotted scouting locations in

00:03:54.840 --> 00:04:01.840
Spain, which essentially doubles for the terrain
you find in Dorne. In support of this assumption,

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:08.890
there have been casting calls for 12 new characters
from the books. Most of them are Martell characters

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:12.250
from Dorne. The rest are all scattered at
various locations.

00:04:12.250 --> 00:04:19.250
Starting with Oberyn's family though. Number
1 - Prince Doran Martell, he's the ruler

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:26.130
in Dorne, but he has gout which makes it hard
for him to walk. Which is why he sent Oberyn

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:31.800
to King's Landing in episode 1. On the show
he just said he was ill and sent his regrets.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:35.360
He's in his 50s, very smart and very powerful.

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.690
He's not like Tywin Lannister though, I
always thought of him as being a lot more

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:43.860
calculating. He's not evil though. Just
very wise.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:49.440
Then there's Trystane Martell, he's Prince
Doran's youngest son. When Tyrion arranged

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:54.210
for Mryrcella to go to Dorne in Season 2,
he also arranged for her and Trystane to become

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.220
Betrothed.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:05:02.220
Then there's the Sand Snakes. Some of them,
there are 8 of them total. They're Oberyn

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:09.130
Martell's bastard daughters. He mentioned
them to Cersei when they were walking in the

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.810
Garden during episode 6.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:17.810
They're all born of septas, common and high
born women. But the one thing they all share

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:25.850
in common is they have Oberyn's eyes. The
nickname Sand Snakes is just a riff on Oberyn's

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:27.440
nickname The Red Viper.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.780
The ones the show is casting include Obara,
who I always thought of as the unofficial

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:38.780
leader of their group, she was also raised
as a fighter. So she's like Brienne levels

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.560
of badass, with a very hot temper.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:49.590
The other Sand Snakes are Nymeria and Tyene.
Both not quite as hot headed as Obara, but

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:50.289
also very deadly.

00:05:50.289 --> 00:05:55.949
Then there's Areo Hotah, he's kind of
like Barristan Selmy. He's Prince Doran's

00:05:55.949 --> 00:05:59.240
personal bodyguard, who has been with him
for a long long time.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:03.750
The other Season 5 characters, aren't Martell
or Dorne characters, so here they are in no

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:05.199
particular order:

00:06:05.199 --> 00:06:09.590
There's Septa Unella. She's part of a
special group of religious leaders in Kings

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:12.479
Landing that rule on matters of faith.

00:06:12.479 --> 00:06:16.199
The High Septon, who is the head of the faith
of the seven in King's Landing. He's like

00:06:16.199 --> 00:06:19.050
the pope for that faith.

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:24.560
Lollys Stokeworth, who everyone will remember
Bronn talking about having just wed. She was

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.520
also a book character that had a bunch of
moments they cut out of the show.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:34.520
Maggy The Frog. She is a fortuneteller from
Cersei's past in Lannisport. When Cersei

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:39.050
was a little girl she went to her for a reading.
She basically gave her this really horrific

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:44.099
prophecy about her future. The character is
supposed to make a brief appearance. So maybe

00:06:44.099 --> 00:06:48.110
there will be a flashback, because she was
supposed to be pretty old when Cersei went

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.990
to see her as a child.

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:55.750
There's Yezzan, who's a slaver in Meereen.
and then there's the Waif.

